					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-217181#post-1890625</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-217181/one-bad-mother#post-1890625</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 12 Nov 2013 05:04:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Captain Cain</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1522769</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>All of the comments seem to be of the exact same caliber.</p> <p>This really is one of the most amazing tales on the site. It completely fulfills my headcanon of Mann, and even though I'm not too familiar with Kald, it easily conveys the character. And it's written so well that instead of trudging along, you get more and more excited to read each month's development, stopping just in time to avoid reaching the 'come on, now. That's enough,' point.</p> <p>I think most intrinsically funny is how insane and desensitized they all are to it&#8230; if it wasn't written to be funny, this stuff would be the darkest nightmare fuel for the writers of the horror franchise. And it makes perfect sense for the psychopathic surgeons to treat this all with the 'Oh, hell. This is gonna suck,' attitude, when anyone else would be beyond terror.</p> <p>I don't even know. I think writing down my thoughts was a mistake, since all there is to say is how great this piece is.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
